A FILTERED TRANSCLUSION CARRIES FIVE OPTIONAL PARTS, and the host binds two of them under names no
reader would guess: the run after the closing braces becomes `style`, and the dotted run after that
becomes `itemClass`.

A tooltip: {{{ [tag[Done]] |a tooltip}}} here.

A suffix, which binds as the style: {{{ [tag[Done]] }}suffix} here.

A class, which binds as the item class: {{{ [tag[Done]] }}}.my-class here.

Every part at once: {{{ [tag[Done]] |a tooltip||A/Template}}suffix}.my-class here.

A PIPE INSIDE THE FILTER ENDS THE FILTER. The host splits on the first one, so the run below binds
`[tag[a` as its filter and `b]] ` as its tooltip rather than reading one filter operand:
{{{ [tag[a|b]] }}} here.

An empty filter builds nothing, and the braces read as text: {{{}}} here.
